aeger isn\'t running or isn\'t configured to accept OTLP traffic on that port, that would explain why the product-catalog service is getting connection refused errors. \n\nTherefore, the right tool here is `exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd` with the command to retrieve the logs of the correct Jaeger pod. This will help confirm if Jaeger is the root cause of the OTLP connection issue.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \ntool description: The correct Jaeger pod name is now identified as `jaeger-6d6f47c768-cwnk8`. I will retrieve its logs to confirm if it is running and listening on port 4317 (OTLP endpoint). This will verify if Jaeger is the root cause of the connection refusal errors observed in the product-catalog service.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl logs jaeger-6d6f47c768-cwnk8 -n astronomy-shop"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=417, prompt_tokens=5791, total_tokens=6208, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd25-7cb0-70f1-9bf1-e11fb78a9bf6-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5791, 'output_tokens': 417, 'total_tokens': 6208}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='14fd3c26-a1bd-48ac-bf27-0524a74bbff9')]]
