t service otel-collector-agent -n astronomy-shop -o yaml would show the spec section, which includes the selector and the deployment name. That way, they can find the correct deployment name and then check its status and logs. \n\nSo the correct tool call here is to get the service\'s YAML to find the associated deployment. Once they have the right deployment name, they can then check the deployment\'s status, logs, or events to find out why the pods aren\'t running.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \ntool description: Execute `kubectl get service otel-collector-agent -n astronomy-shop -o yaml` to inspect the service\'s spec and identify the correct deployment or pod name it is referencing. This will clarify whether the service is misconfigured or pointing to a non-existent deployment.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl get service otel-collector-agent -n astronomy-shop -o yaml"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 537, 'prompt_tokens': 3903, 'total_tokens': 4440, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd24-b5db-7140-a2a1-b1332e66c48e-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3903, 'output_tokens': 537, 'total_tokens': 4440}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='8fc5e137-0af9-4bc4-ad67-8dc2afc7d002'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what's going on here. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the OpenTelemetry Collector in their Kubernetes cluster. The product-catalog service is having trouble connecting to the OTLP endpoint, which is supposed to be handled by the otel-collector-agent. \n\nEarlier steps showed that the otel-collector-agent pods aren't running, and when they tried to check the deployment, it wasn't found. Now, the user is trying to get the service YAML for otel-collector-agent. The service exists, but the deployment might be misconfigured or the service is pointing to the wrong pods.\n\nLooking at the service YAML, the key thing is the selector. If the service's selector doesn't match any pods, that means the service isn't properly routing traffic to the collector. The user needs to check the service's spec to see if the selector is correct. For example, if the service is supposed to target pods with a label like app=otel-collector-agent, but those pods don't exist, the service won't work. \n\nAlso, the user should verify if the deployment name in the service's spec matches an existing deployment. If the deployment was renamed or deleted, the service would be pointing to nothing. Additionally, checking the endpoints associated with the service could show if there are any IP addresses and ports listed, which would indicate if the service is correctly connected to pods.\n\nSo, the next step is to inspect the service's YAML to check the selector and deployment references. This will help determine why the service isn't finding the necessary pods and how to correct the configuration.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get service otel-collector-agent -n astronomy-shop -o yaml"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b60a8674f10af1b8', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 372, 'prompt_tokens': 4912, 'total_tokens': 5284, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run-