ger's ExternalName is pointing to a non-existent service, causing the OTLP endpoint to be unreachable. That's the main problem here.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get services -n astronomy-shop"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9c46161bcfe0f069', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 353, 'prompt_tokens': 3312, 'total_tokens': 3665, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd28-1e56-7873-880d-e917ae791638-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get services -n astronomy-shop'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9c46161bcfe0f069', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3312, 'output_tokens': 353, 'total_tokens': 3665}), ToolMessage(content='NAME                  TYPE           CLUSTER-IP       EXTERNAL-IP                                PORT(S)                                                            AGE\nad                    ClusterIP      10.99.86.111     <none>                                     8080/TCP                                                           7m23s\ncart                  ClusterIP      10.97.160.70     <none>                                     8080/TCP                                                           7m23s\ncheckout              ClusterIP      10.104.234.179   <none>                                     8080/TCP                                                           7m23s\ncurrency              ClusterIP      10.111.16.94     <none>                                     8080/TCP                                                           7m23s\nemail                 ClusterIP      10.106.148.168   <none>      