source managing the otel-collector service. If it\'s a Deployment, they can get the deployment info. If it\'s a StatefulSet, they need to check that. \n\nIn any case, the key is to verify the deployment and pod status for otel-collector to determine why the service isn\'t functioning as expected. Once that\'s clear, they can address the root cause, whether it\'s a deployment issue, misconfigured labels, or other problems.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely  \n**Reasoning:** The absence of pods labeled `app=otel-collector` indicates that the `otel-collector` service may not be properly deployed or configured. To diagnose this, we need to inspect the deployment or statefulset managing the `otel-collector` service to verify its configuration, replica status, and any potential errors.  \n\ntool_call:  \n{\n  "tool": "exec_kubectl_cmd_safely",\n  "command": "kubectl get deployment -n astronomy-shop -l app=otel-collector"\n}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=824, prompt_tokens=4063, total_tokens=4887, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd28-d516-7433-bc92-c7636592c3ba-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4063, 'output_tokens': 824, 'total_tokens': 4887}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='999d5fe2-d296-4b9d-9e5d-ef627344c4bc')]]
